,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 3.6.2\n- Reproducible in Godot 3.5\n\n### System information\n\nlinux (Debian 13.5)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen setting the Loop Offset parameter in an imported mp3 or ogg file, the parameter is ignored and it gets reset upon starting the game or closing and reopening the editor.\nEven manually editing the `.import` file doesn't help.\n\nNote that launching the game after editing the loop offset and looking at the AudioStreamPlayer in the Remote tab shows the loop offset properly set, however the audio file just loops back to 0.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- import an audio file (tried with mp3 or ogg)\n- open it with the inspector\n- set the Loop Offset (in my case I set it e.g. to `11.1`)\n- set the audio file as the source stream for an AudioStreamPlayer, set to Autoplay=true\n- start the game and hear that the loop offset is not honored\n- restart the editor\n- notice that the Loop Offset is now 0\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[repro_loop_offset.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29937979/repro_loop_offset.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121273/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}